{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_0","type":"agent_message","text":"{
  "readings": [
    {
      "local_id": "classification_trigger",
      "family": "modality",
      "subject": "Selected control: whether the retained circular triggers complex-product treatment for distribution of a particular Fund",
      "statement": "[TRUE_IS_SATISFIED] For an SFC-authorised fund offered to the public in Hong Kong that is not a listed closed-ended alternative asset fund, the classification trigger is satisfied when its aggregate direct and indirect exposure to private market assets is at least 50% of NAV, or when the SFC has actually designated it as a complex product on a case-by-case basis. True means that this circular supplies a basis requiring complex-product treatment for distribution. False, within scope and with the relevant facts established, means that neither classification route is established under this selected control; it does not establish non-complex status under every other applicable rule. Missing exposure or designation evidence remains unknown. The retained text supports one classification structure; the principal unresolved issues concern exposure measurement, timing and evidence, rather than a competing rule making every private-market exposure automatically complex.",
      "distinction": "The threshold sentence uses mandatory language, while the below-threshold route requires an SFC designation and permits a holistic assessment. For example, an in-scope Fund with established aggregate exposure of exactly 50% satisfies the trigger without a separate designation. A Fund at 49% with established absence of an SFC designation does not satisfy this selected trigger merely because its CLO holdings or liquidity profile warrant scrutiny; a Fund at 49% that has actually been designated does satisfy it. An otherwise comparable LAF falls outside this circular's defined Fund scope. A Fund whose exposure or designation history is missing cannot be treated as the established 49%-and-undesignated case. Footnote 7 supports attaching holistic assessment to cases below 50%, rather than making the express 50% threshold discretionary. The strongest uncertainty is how to establish aggregate exposure for layered instruments and the relevant assessment date.",
      "citations": [
        {
          "unit_id": "d4148dd852cee.u4.564",
          "quote": "This circular provides guidance to management companies of funds that are authorised by the SFC for offering to the public in Hong Kong (Funds)6 in this regard."
        },
        {
          "unit_id": "d4148dd852cee.u63.8691",
          "quote": "Except for listed closed-ended alternative asset funds (LAFs)."
        },
        {
          "unit_id": "d4148dd852cee.u21.3779",
          "quote": "A Fund will be considered as a complex product if its total direct and indirect exposures to private market assets amount to 50% or more of the Fund’s NAV."
        },
        {
          "unit_id": "d4148dd852cee.u21.3779",
          "quote": "On a case-by-case basis, the SFC may also designate a Fund as a complex product, taking into account factors including, without limitation:"
        },
        {
          "unit_id": "d4148dd852cee.u29.4630",
          "quote": "In assessing whether the complex product designation is warranted7, the SFC will adopt a holistic approach taking into account the specific circumstances of the case."
        },
        {
          "unit_id": "d4148dd852cee.u64.8910",
          "quote": "In cases where the Fund’s aggregate direct and indirect exposures to private market assets are less than 50% of the Fund’s NAV."
        },
        {
          "unit_id": "d4148dd852cee.u32.4805",
          "quote": "A Fund classified as a complex product will be subject to the SFC’s prevailing requirements for the sale of complex products8 including but not limited to ensuring the suitability of the Fund for its investors irrespective of whether solicitation or recommendation is involved."
        },
        {
          "unit_id": "d4148dd852cee.u49.6955",
          "quote": "Fund managers are encouraged to consult the SFC at the earliest opportunity if they are in doubt regarding complex product classification of their Funds."
        }
      ],
      "assumptions": [
        "The formalization evaluates one particular fund at one identified assessment time; it does not determine whole-firm compliance or satisfaction of the downstream sales requirements.",
        "Footnote 6 qualifies the defined population of Funds, and footnote 7 qualifies the holistic designation assessment in cases below 50%.",
        "The designation fact records an actual, applicable SFC designation. A manager's view that designation is likely or appropriate does not establish that fact.",
        "The threshold fact must be established using a supportable exposure measurement. The formalization supplies no missing valuation, look-through, aggregation or monitoring convention.",
        "A result is interpreted only within the Boolean scope. Unknown facts are not assigned false values; one established true classification route can nevertheless establish the result without resolving the other route."
      ],
      "questions": [
        "How should indirect exposure through BDCs, CLOs, TRSs and SRTs be measured and aggregated, including look-through, derivative exposure and possible double counting?",
        "What valuation date, monitoring frequency and treatment of temporary threshold crossings govern the 50% test?",
        "What evidence establishes an applicable SFC designation, its effective date and any subsequent withdrawal or replacement?",
        "Does omitted commencement or transitional material specify when existing Funds must complete classification changes and distributor communications?"
      ],
